Make the stack size of drogon's IO event loop threads configurable

drogon runs request handlers on its IO event loop threads. trantor
starts those threads with std::thread, so they get the OS default stack
size (about 512 KiB on macOS). RonSQL recurses deeply when it processes
deeply nested queries and overflowed that stack (RONDB-1016).

This patch adds HttpAppFramework::setThreadStackSize() and passes the
size through trantor's EventLoopThreadPool to EventLoopThread, which
starts its thread with pthread_create instead of std::thread so that the
stack size can be set. A size of 0 keeps the OS default. rdrs2 sets
8 MiB in server/src/main.cc.

